                                    Load Balancing
                                         ------> ELB in AWS

AWS Load Balancer: Region
target group --> backend servers


GCP Load balancer: Global
instance group --> backend servers

**Steps to create Load balancer
1. create Instance group ---> target group
2. create instance template  
3. create Load balncer
 ---> select LB --> application / network
 ---> select internal or public facing
 ---> select global or regional

 4. configure LB
 --> LB name
 --> select Region
 --> select network--> VPC
 --> create proxy subnet
 -----> it is a special internal network used by GCP LB to send traffic to backend VMs

 --> frontend configure
 --> backend configure
 --> done

